    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0654" n="633" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.811/7–2948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kohler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-29">July 29, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1450. Soviet press July 29 announces air departure of Soviet Delegation to Danube
                    Conference headed by Vishinsky; Deputy Minister Merchant Marine S. M. Bayev;
                    Deputy Minister Foreign Trade S. A. Bor[i]sov; Ambassador to Yugoslavia A. I.
                    Lavrentyev; and Deputy Director of Balkan Countries Section of Ministry Foreign
                    Affairs, Minister Plenipotentiary S. P. Kirsanov. Belgrade Tass despatch
                    announces arrival Ukrainian Delegation headed by Comrade Baranovski.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d406-f1"/> Size delegations not given.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d406-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent Department 1450, repeated Belgrade 52.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kohler</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d406-f1" n="1" xml:id="d406-f1-content">
                <p>Anatol Maximovich Baranovsky was the Deputy Chairman of the Council of Ministers
                    of the Ukrainian Soviet Socialist Republic.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d406-f2" n="2" xml:id="d406-f2-content">
                <p>The arrival of Vyshinsky, Ana Pauker, and others in Belgrade during the afternoon
                    of July 29 was reported in telegram 1017 from Belgrade on July 30, 1948.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
